# Copy to .env and edit. The STELLA backend works with NO edits (sane defaults);
# everything below is optional. There is no LLM and no cloud provider to configure -
# intent is decided by a local embedding classifier baked into the image.

# --- Intent classifier (local static-embedding model; CPU, no LLM) ---
# Baked into the image at build time. Override only to use a different model2vec model.
# STELLA_CLASSIFIER_MODEL=minishlab/potion-base-32M

# --- TTS engine (default: piper, self-contained in the image) ---
# Both the ack and chat routes default to piper. The optional host-side Chatterbox
# clone service (see voice/) is legacy and off by default; point a route at it only if
# you actually run that service and reach it at STELLA_CHATTERBOX_URL.
# STELLA_TTS_ACK_ENGINE=piper
# STELLA_TTS_CHAT_ENGINE=piper
# STELLA_CHATTERBOX_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8123

# --- Optional API token (defense in depth on a shared network) ---
# When set, every server route except /health requires 'Authorization: Bearer <token>'.
# The client sends it automatically when its own config has the same value. Unset =
# open (fine for a single-PC loopback setup). Use a long random string.
# STELLA_API_TOKEN=change_me_to_a_long_random_string
